  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 821 PM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nA stout upper ridge as well as high pressure to our northeast over \nthe Appalachians will keep most shower and storm activity out of the \nforecast (aside from perhaps low chances over the terrain) through \nthe next week. Therefore, hot and humid conditions will continue to \nbe the theme next week with forecast highs in the lower to mid 90s, \nlows in the lower to mid 70s, and dew points in the upper 60s to \nlower 70s each day. This will result in Heat Indices ranging between \n100-107 degrees each day, along with NWS HeatRisk in the Moderate to \nMajor (Levels 2 and 3 of 4) categories every day and WBGTs in the mid\nto upper 80s each afternoon. We'll need to keep an eye to see if any\nheat products will be necessary; however, regardless, please \npractice heat safety! This is especially important if you work \noutdoors or have outdoor activities. Make sure to dress in light- \ncolored, loose-fitting clothing, drink plenty of water, and take \nfrequent breaks in the shade. Also, never leave people or pets in \nvehicles!",
